ntdll: Manage memory in the JIT arena and the app's address space.

virtual.c, in dependency order:
- the JIT arena: views written through the arena's write alias,
  one-way protection, ios_app_vm_call for executable memory a program
  allocates (ordinary memory, which only FEX reads)
- PE images mapped through the alias, and the x18 to x28 rewrite of
  images that use x18
- the ARM64EC map, sized to fit
- the large-allocation pool (bigpool), host-slack bounce and the
  kernel-choice fallback in map_free_area
- the thread-stack pool and the swap file (KITSUNE_SWAP)
- soft pools for CEF, the mid-size bands, sub-reservations and the
  relocation of hinted reservations into the band
- Win32 error codes as Windows returns them, so retry loops end
- child exit reclaim: views and pool members owned by a child are freed
  when it exits (ios_reclaim_owner_arena_views); syscall.c attributes
  allocations and mappings to the child that made them
- diagnostics: address-space census, reports and the fault-loop
  detector
kernelbase's GetPhysicallyInstalledSystemMemory rounds up to a whole GB.

The soft pools are adapted from Madeira (willfaust/Madeira 69496fd).
